Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  51   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 14 09  Results To   Kevin S  Hughes MD  Chien Wei Eric Liao MD  PhD    FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT     Invasive ductal carcinoma with extensive dermal involvement     Metastatic carcinoma in 10 of 11 axillary lymph nodes and multinodular  axillary soft tissue involvement     Ductal carcinoma in situ with calcifications     Fibrocystic changes and sclerosing adenosis with calcifications     Focal areas of fibrosis in parenchyma  skin  and lymph nodes consistent with  therapy effect     See note and tables  1 and  2     NOTE  Although focal areas of fibrosis consistent with therapy effect are  present  there is abundant residual invasive carcinoma both in the parenchyma  and skin  The overall grade is 2  tubule formation   2  nuclear pleomorphism    2  mitotic activity   3   but this does not quite reflect the morphologic  heterogeneity that is present  This heterogeneity is represented by many areas  that appear grade 1  some areas that appear grade 2  and scattered areas with  poor tubule formation and high mitotic activity  which would warrant a grade of  3 if viewed in isolation  Focal tumoral necrosis and minor extracellular mucin  production are also noted       TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA    Tumor Size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with multiple subcentimeter satellite nodules   Grade  2  see note above    Lymphatic Vessel Invasion  Suspicious for a focus of dermal lymphatic invasion   Blood Vessel Invasion  Not identified   Perineural Invasion  Present   Margin of Invasive Carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma comes to 0 15cm from the  medial skin margin in one focus  The remaining skin margins and parenchymal  margins are  0 2cm away   Location of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  Within the region of the mass   Grade of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  2 to focal 3   Margin of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm  or greater   Stains for Receptors  Requested       TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2  SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES    Total Number of Positive Lymph Nodes  10  Total Number of Lymph Nodes Examined  11    Number with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0    Number with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   2    Number with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   8  Extracapsular Extension  Marked   Other Forms of Axillary Involvement  Lymphatic vessels and multifocal soft  tissue metastases              Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD         PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note       Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision            Electronically Signed Out By  Atul K Bhan MBBS  MD on REMOVED_DATE 13 22       CLINICAL HISTORY  Right breast cancer  Stitches  Short superior  long lateral     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    right breast    axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy  specimen with a short stitch designating superior   a long stitch designating  lateral  and attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axilla  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm  tan white skin is thickened with several areas of deep  irregular retraction and  puckering and pink yellow plaques  The skin abnormalities are present in all  four quadrants but are especially prominent in the inferior aspect of the  specimen  The nipple areolar complex appears firm   granular with pink brown  areas of discoloration  The anterior margin is inked blue   the posterior  margin is inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  poorly defined  firm  grey white mass spanning almost the entire length of the  specimen from medial to lateral  which underlies the aforementioned skin  puckering  and comes to 2 6cm of the posterior margin and 3 8cm of the  anterior margin  Also noted surrounding the lesion are multiple i