sults of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lump  is a 4 x 4 x 1 5cm breast specimen that is inked black laterally  red on its deep resection margin  blue superiorly  green inferiorly  It is sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm mass with an irregular border that is 0 3cm from the closest margin  the deep margin   A portion is saved for Dr  Dennis Sgroi  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through L  with the nodule in cassettes D through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan blue lymph node with a small amount of associated adipose tissue  The lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary node  non sentinel  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink node with a small amount of associated adipose tissue  The lymph node is bisected and submitted in its entirety in cassette N  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPOR