Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   CRIBIFORM TYPE  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  DUCTAL E IRHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  DUCT ECTASIA  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The infiltrating tumor component measures 0 9cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  slide A   No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section gross impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 20 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with needle localizing wire in place  and accompanying specimen roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a single  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm area of dense tissue surrounded by yellow  soft  lobulated adipose tissue  The suspicious area extends to the ink  and is located in the mid portion of the thickened segment of the wire  The lesion is too small to freeze  and no frozen section is done  Submitted entirely in A through J  with the lesion in A and B  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
