Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma  pleomorphic type who is status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy undergoing left breast lumpectomy and left axillary dissection  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION 1  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS 2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE 3  MILD USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS   DISSECTION 1  TWENTY ONE LYMPH NODES WITH NO TUMOR IDENTIFIED  0 21  2  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND CAVITARY FAT NECROSIS C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FOCAL RESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM 2  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS GREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION 3  FOCAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  4  FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS SEE NOTE  D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS E  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS F  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN DEEP   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS G  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS H  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS 2  SCLEROSING FIBROADENOMA I  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL   EXCISION 1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE 2  FOCAL FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA 3  SCLEROSING FIBROADENOMA 4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS Note  Sections of the left breast excision  part A  reveal a small focus of lobular carcinoma in situ  LCIS  measuring approximately 0 2cm  The lobules in this focus are distended by a proliferation of large pleomorphic cells exhibiting changes secondary to prior neoadjuvant therapy  These cells are enlarged with a moderate amount of dense cytoplasm and enlarged hyperchromatic  eccentrically placed nuclei  Sections of the left breast final margin inferior medial  part C   reveal a single microscopic focus of invasive lobular carcinoma  present as a small cluster of single cells in densely sclerotic stroma  The tumor cells are large with abundant cytoplasm and eccentrically placed hyperchromatic nuclei and are morphologically similar to the cells present in the focus of LCIS described for part A  The focus of invasive lobular carcinoma measures 0 2cm and is located greater than 0 2cm from the closest margin  No other focus of invasive carcinoma is present in any of the specimens submitted  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin performed on sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show negative staining in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and support the diagnosis  An immunohistochemical stain for cytokeratin performed on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights the lobular carcinoma cells  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast lumpectomy with needle localization  short stitch superior and long stitch lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm oriented fragment of breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place and a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  There is a metallic clip on the posterior aspect  located 1 5cm from the