Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 94 at 11 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  LOW GRADE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN A TINY FOCUS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension and displays moderate stromal cellularity  In regions  the tumor has an infiltrative border  and the tumor cells extend to the margin of the specimen in one small area  The tumor cells do not show either atypia or mitotic activity  Stromal overgrowth is not present  These findings suggest a low likelihood for recurrence and metastasis  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 MAY 94 at 12 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a fairly well demarcated lesion  REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in maximum dimension and extending to within 1mm of the inked margin  The lesion is tan gray  bulging and mobile  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted in cassette L  A section representing the lesion with the closest margin is submitted in cassette A  the lesion in cassettes B through G  remainder of the specimen is cassettes H through K  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  FAVOR BENIGN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Christopher S Ogilvy  M D  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 41 CLINICAL DATA  Diagnosed by core biopsy at Brigham and Women s Hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTEROLATERAL AND REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTEROSUPERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite angiolymphatic invasion is seen  There are calcifications associated with the carcinoma in situ  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN IN THE INFERO ANTERIOR REGION  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISION  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 14 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lump   is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of breast  with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and short stitch designating the superior aspect  There is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hemorrhagic biopsy site which extends within 0 4cm of the posterior margin  and an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nodular  firm  pink mass with focal hemorrhage  biopsy site   The mass is less than 0 1cm from the anterolateral margin  and REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm from the posterosuperior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is fatty with an area of hemorrhage in the inferior region  SECTION CODE A B  Mass and posterosuperior margin  C D  Mass approaching anterolateral margin  E  Representative central sections of mass  There is a 0 4cm cystic focus adjacent to the mass where it approaches the posterosuperior margin  and is included in cassette B  Also noted in the inferoanterior aspect  is an approximately 2 0cm in greatest dimension region with prominent ducts with focal punctate yellow areas  representatives in cassette F  G is from unremarkable fatty tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary lymph nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm fragment of fatty tissue with numerous lymph nodes  of up to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  in cassettes H through K  Labeled  left breast  additional margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable breast fragment with a black stitch designating the edge furthest from tumor  The entire specimen surface on which the edge is stitched is inked black  with the opposing surface inked blue  The breast tissue in the stitched region has dense  white parenchyma and is submitted entirely in L through N  with representative sections of the remaining fatty parenchyma in O through Q  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     NO GROSS DIAGNOSIS RENDERED  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
