Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral simple mastectomies  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   2  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SMALL INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITES  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  2  FIBROCYSTIC AND FIBROADENOMATOUS CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SKIN TAG OF THE NIPPLE  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME     REMOVED_DATE  Received fresh  labeled with  left breast  stitch at 6 o clock   is a 25 x 20 x 2 5cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 6 o clock  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nipple  which are both grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial lateral axis to reveal two biopsy sites  The first REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan white biopsy site lies approximately in the central quadrant of the breast  is associated with a metallic clip  and is located 5 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 2 5cm from the closest anterior margin  Approximately 5cm lateral to this  is the second REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white biopsy site  which is located in the outer quadrant of the breast  0 3cm from closest posterior margin and 1cm from the closest anterior margin  The breast parenchyma between the 2 biopsy sites has a tan yellow lobulated unremarkable cut surface  The remaining parenchyma of the specimen contains tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue with no discrete mass or lesion  The upper outer quadrant tissue is also palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First biopsy site  entirely submitted  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Second biopsy site  entirely submitted  with closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma between the 2 biopsy sites   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the breast parenchyma of the upper inner quadrant  Received fresh  labeled with  right breast  stitch at 12 o clock   is a 26 x 21 x 3 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unremarkable areola and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm nipple  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan brown papilliferous skin nodule  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial lateral axis to reveal a predominantly tan yellow lobulated cut surface interspersed with a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  No discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is also palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the breast parenchyma are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the breast parenchyma of the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the skin nodule of the nipple  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 09   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 14 33PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
