ension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  LYMPH NODE MUSCLE  RIGHT INTERPECTORAL   EXCISION  NUMEROUS NODULES   20  OF INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA INVOLVING SKELETAL MUSCLE AND ADIPOSE TISSUE  LYMPHATIC INVASION PRESENT  SEE NOTE   Note  Although round  the tumor nodules do not show evidence of underlying lymph nodes  The findings are more suggestive of soft tissue deposits as a result of lymphatic spread  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with an REMOVED_DATE x8 0 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced anteriorly by a REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm skin ellipse  There is a short stitch on the superior aspect of the ellipse and a long stitch on the lateral aspect of the ellipse as per the surgeon s note  The skin is pale tan with diffuse light pink mottling  a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areolar complex and 1 2cm in diameter nipple  The areolar complex and nipple are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm ill defined area of tan white firm nodularity  The nodules range in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm  This mass is approximately 3 0cm from the lateral aspect of the specimen and 3 0cm from the closest posterior margin  The mass comes to within 3 0cm of the skin  The mass is greater than 3 0cm from all other margins  A representative section of the closest posterior margin to mass is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of fibroadipose tissue with interspersed fibrous septae  A representative section of lateral uninvolved breast parenchyma is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   a representative section of medial uninvolved