ROM THE MARGIN DESIGNATED BY A SUTURE ALONG A REMOVED_DATE CM FRONT  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinal lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm specimen of fat that contains a lymph node  The fat is removed and the lymph node is bisected and frozen as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm left breast excisional breast specimen  The surgeon denotes the lateral border of the specimen with a long stitch and the superior border of the specimen with the short stitch  The specimen is inked as follows  superior green  inferior yellow  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is received with the localization wire outside of the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  Approximally 0 8cm from the medial border  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm solid whitish pink nodule with punctate hemorrhage which is not encapsulated  This nodule is 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 2cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the inferior margin  1 4cm from the superior margin  and  2 0cm from the lateral margin  The following cassettes are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   serial sectioning from the medial border to past the described nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   serial sectioning from the medial margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Best look at described nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   continued serial sectioning  the superior margin is truncated off such that the section can fit in the cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Continued serial sectioning such that sectioning appears to have proceeded lateral to the nodule  the nodule will not be seen in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The most lateral part of the specimen appears unremarkable  and the entire specimen is not submitted  The entire nodule is submitted however  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   medial posterior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm dome shaped soft tissue specimen with a stitch placed by the surgeon denoting the plane of the new margin  The new margin is inked black  This new margin does have an area of fibrous white tissue on part of its surface  Underlying the inked margin there is yellowish fatty tissue with interspersed white fibrous tissue  This specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The majority   90   of the specimen is submitted  Gross Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT MEDIAL POSTERIOR MARGIN   E