f staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Specimen received fresh in the Frozen SectiOn Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mass with an ill defined lobular mass which lies within 0 1cm of several inked surfaces  Representative tissue samples are submitted in cassettes A to F with closest margins in A and B  tumor in C and D and other suspicious areas in E and F  Gross Description by  ANTHONY FORRESTER  HMS Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
