Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 20 CLINICAL DATA  Prior left lumpectomy  XRT  REMOVED_CASE_ID   local recurrence  Left mastectomy  tissue expander placement                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 18 57                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  Serial sectioning reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  The biopsy cavity comes to 1 2cm from the anterior margin and 2 0cm from the posterior margin  There is a firm white fibrotic tissue superior  anterior  and inferior to the biopsy cavity  abutting the anterior margin and coming within 1 6cm from the posterior margin  The remaining specimen consist of 85  lobulated yellow lobulated fat and 15  fibrous tissue  A  anterior section of biopsy cavity B  posterior section of biopsy cavity C  superior section of biopsy cavity D  additional representative section of biopsy cavity E F  representative section of fibrofatty tissue away from cavity Resident  NICOLE ANN BELSLEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 40 CLINICAL DATA  Question of cancer by mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 4CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 0 2CM OF AN INKED SURFACE  AND WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  DefinIte blood vascular invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE  B  BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   1  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA HYPERPLASIA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The margins of resection are free of carcinoma  and atypical hyperplasia  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 2 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white area measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  0 2cm from the closest margin  A representative section from the suspicious area is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder of the lesion is in B D  Additional representative sections of the surrounding tissue are in E and F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and a 6 0cm sutured recent incision  The specimen is irregular  such that there is significantly more tissue in the superior lateral region  In addition  posterior to the ellipse  beneath the recent incision is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm apparently exposed biopsy cavity  which is inked green  The margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal soft white parenchyma in the region of the biopsy cavity  The closest margin to the biopsy site is 1cm  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty  with an area of localized fibrous and cystic change  1 0cm inferior and medial to the nipple  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted from medial to lateral in G K  with margin  Representative sections of the cystic area  medial to the biopsy cavity are in L and M  Unremarkable tissue away from the cavity is in N  The axillary tissue is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in O V  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
