Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 46 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  SINGLE FOCUS SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue  This specimen has 3 stitches  1 short and 1 long marking the superficial portion  2 long stitches marking the superior margin and 2 short stitches marking the medial margin  This specimen is inked black and red  over black in the superior area and medial areas  Sectioning discloses a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm spiculated hard area spanning the superior margin  within REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm of it  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 now submitted in cassette H  The specimen is entirely submitted with the superficial portion in cassette A and B  the deep  or inferior portion  in G  and the remainder submitted entirely from superficial to deep in C F  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 RIGHT BREAST RESECTION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
