uring REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  The brown  wrinkled unremarkable areola measures 3 2cm in diameter and the brown  wrinkled inverted nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  There is a scant amount of axillary tail on the lateral aspect  denoted by a suture  as per the surgeon  5 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm    The specimen is additionally received with a short suture denoting the superior aspect of the specimen  as per the surgeon  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  Upon sectioning  there is a white pink  firm cavity in the upper inner quadrant measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  filled with gritty packing material and located 0 5cm from the anterior margin and 3 1cm from the posterior margin  There is an ill defined fibrous  gritty area adjacent to the LIQ cavity  Further sectioning reveals an additional pink gray  smooth lined  puckered  firm area in the lower outer quadrant  possibly consistent with a previous biopsy site  3 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm    This area is focally abutting the posterior margin  and extending focally to abut the anterior margin  There is an ill defined  fibrous nodule   approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm    located 0 5cm from the lower outer quadrant cavity  1 2cm from the anterior margin and 3 0cm from the posterior margin  The remaining cut surfaces consist of a dense  edematous  focally nodular fibrous tissue  approximately 50  of the cut surfaces   and yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  The scant amount of axillary tissue is dissected and palpated to reveal a single possible lymph node measuring 0 4cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previous biopsy site in upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Possible previous biopsy site in lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is one section  cut in half to demonstrate posterior and anterior margin relationship    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area adjacent to UIQ cavity  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area  0 5cm from LOQ cavity Received fresh  labeled  left breast  additional left axillary contents   is an irregular portion of yellow  lobulated fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  which is dissected and palpated to reveal 17 possible lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  All possible nodes are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing one possible lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four possible lymph nodes  submitted entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two possible lymph nodes  submitted entirely  Additional E cadherin Immunohistochemistry Results  Repeat e cadherin immunohistochemistry stains on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveal that the invasive carcinoma cells stain for membrane e cadherin  This result supports a diagnosis of invasive ductal rather than invasive lobular carcinoma  Repeat e cadherin stains on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveal that the majority of the in situ carcinoma is ductal carcinoma in situ with a minor lobular carcinoma in situ component  Both invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma extend to less than 0 2cm from the inked anterior margin  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Dennis Sgroi M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  2 by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT ADDITIONAL AXILLA   DISSECTION  report_end  , Unchecked.
