etermined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for p63  myosin  calponin and keratin were performed on sections  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and confirm the presence of an invasive component  The previously reported diagnosis remains unchanged  Addendum  2 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  3 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  98  to chromosome 17 signals  96  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 44 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON THE MICROSCOPIC SLIDE  95   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  5   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  DUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  The inked specimen margin appears free of tumor  however  tumor extends within fractions of a millimeter of the margin  Vascular invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue with two needle localizations  Taking the area where the needles exit the specimen as the proximal end  the specimen is inked  the needles removed  and the specimen is sectioned proximal to distal to reveal a hard  white to tan 6mm nodule approximately 2mm from the nearest inked margin  which corresponds to a prominent mammographic lesion  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through M  Cassette A represents the most proximal portion  cassette M represents the most distal portion  and cassettes B through G represent the nodule  No frozen done  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   FIRM SUSPICIOUS LESION 6MM IN DIAMETER  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Paul Clarke Shellito  M D  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Unchecked.
