 of the posterior margin  Abutting the cavity along the lateral aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm gray pink nodule  which comes to 3 0cm of the posterior margin  Also noted 0 6cm superolateral to the cavity is a 2nd REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm region of hemorrhage and fat necrosis  which comes to 2 0cm of the posterior margin  Located 0 3cm medial to the cavity in the mid breast is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm elongated gray white fibrous nodule  which comes to 3 5cm of the posterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays focal nodularity  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  submitted from lateral to medial  with closest posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superomedial nodule entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and small lateral nodule in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Focus of hemorrhage and fat necrosis superolateral to previous biopsy site in the upper outer quadrant  including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodularity in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodularity in medial breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Elongated mid breast fibrous nodule  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right sentinel lymph node    REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  which is dissected to reveal 3 tan pink lymph nodes  The 1st lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The 2nd lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The final lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  inked blue  bisected  and entirely submitted also as FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is 