Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 58 CLINICAL DATA  62 year old female with a positive breast biopsy for invasive ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  3 0CM  PRESENT ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Resection margins appear free of carcinoma  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion not seen  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  16  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 34                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  labeled  left breast  only is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring 24 x 20 x 5 5cm with an associated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse with the nipple at the inferior of the skin ellipse  A 3 2cm  well healed scar is present in the upper inner quadrant  and an associated 0 3cm skin ulcer with white raised borders at one edge of the incision  Attached are the axillary contents which measure 13cm x 10cm x 2cm  There are no palpable masses  The specimen is inked and the axillary dissection is removed for an axillary dissection  and the nodes were submitted in A E  The mastectomy specimen is serially sectioned laterally to medially to reveal some firm  white breast tissue with grossly well defined borders that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  directly under the skin ellipse  Proceeding medially  there is a granular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE firm mass with poorly defined